- Additions to the report: "drag_mode" field + add "drag_mode_api_window_start_drag" to variant_api; log drag samples in both modes for comparison (reuse _drag_samples for A; for B, sample the window position over time? In B mode the engine may not receive movement events, so samples can instead capture the window position on each _process frame — record [t, win.x, win.y]). Maintain a separate array `native_drag_samples` captured in _process while native_drag_active.
- capability_probe.gd already probes for the existence of window_start_drag. It may be extended to record the value of `DisplayServer.window_get_visible_rect`/`window_get_position` — unnecessary.

